(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-6"] = {"468257101":[["","\"In the end, our enemy will be silence.\""],["","Chapter 1"],["","XC 119, March, Lorine Mountains – Vesper Warehouse"],["Arthur","Phew... Arthur, you've got this..."],["","In the empty operations room, Arthur takes a few deep breaths. She reaches out and pats her cheeks, as if trying to pat away the anxiety weighing on her chest."],["Arthur","As long as you explain it properly, everyone will understand..."],["","But what if they still don't?"],["Arthur","Then what am I supposed to..."],["","What if we lose everyone's support?"],["Arthur","Even then, we have to keep fighting..."],["","What if the very people we're trying to protect are bent on destroying themselves?"],["Arthur","..."],["","For now, her answer can only be... take it one step at a time."],["","The doubts in her heart have no outlet, but time is no longer on her side. She puts the questions to one side, pushes open the door, and steps forward to face the clamor outside."],["","But putting doubts to one side does not make them disappear..."],["Arthur","I've said this over and over..."],["Arthur","Before long, the DLAF will turn this pass into a primary assault route. If you stay here, we can't guarantee your safety."],["Refugee A","But... if we leave, we've got nowhere else to go."],["Refugee B","Hah, guarantee our safety? Then why did you set up the base in this mining area to begin with?"],["Arthur","That was to prevent the Dawnstar League from interfering further with mining operations..."],["Refugee B","Well, before you came, the DLAF didn't seem that interested in the mining area..."],["Refugee B","In fact, it was only after you Vesper lot showed up that the DL took action, and now you're thinking of driving us out to build your defenses, right?"],["Arthur","These are necessary defensive measures. Don't worry, we'll find a way to provide accommodation for all of you."],["Refugee A","But this is the home we've spent over a decade building. How can you expect us to just pack up and..."],["Refugee B","Don't waste words on them! We're not leaving—what are they gonna do about it?"],["Arthur","..."],["","Arthur falls into a brief silence. She is a girl with quite a temper, never using words when fists can solve the problem."],["","But now, this is a matter that cannot be solved with fists."],["Arthur","Once the fighting starts, everything will—"],["Refugee B","Then don't fight! Why should we be dragged into this mess you've made?!"],["???","Yeah, exactly, just don't fight. It doesn't have to come to that, does it?"],["Arthur","...And you are?"],["???","Me? Oh, sorry, I think I'm in the wrong place. I'll just leave..."],["Arthur","Freeze!"],["","Arthur takes a deep breath, plunges into the crowd, and grabs the figure trying to escape."],["???","Whoa there, kid. I admire the enthusiasm, but I'm really just passing through."],["Arthur","Although it has been modified, this is obviously an NDF uniform... Cassha has already had the area cordoned off... Why are you here?"],["???","You mean this? Sorry, sorry, just something I picked up and tweaked from a flea market. Pretty common around places like this, right?"],["Refugee B","Skysweep, if you have something you need to do, go ahead. These Vesper never listen."],["Arthur","No, we've never interfered with Free Milkhama in the slightest. You have no reason to say that..."],["Skysweep","Stop, stop. Can't you tell you're only making this worse?"],["Skysweep","<yellow>Mr</yellow>... Er, I mean <yellow>MISS Arthur</yellow>, I suggest you find someone more articulate to mediate."],["Arthur","You...!"],["","It's obvious that this man, relentlessly fanning the flames, is not from Free Milkhama."],["","If she loses composure at a time like this, all the previous efforts to maintain stability will have been in vain."],["","However, the pent-up frustration in one's heart always finds an outlet..."],["Arthur","YAH!"],["","A swift straight punch lands on Skysweep's face, knocking him backward into several onlookers."],["","The originally packed crowd erupts in an uproar, instantly clearing a small space, and leaving only Arthur and Skysweep as the main attraction."],["Arthur","Huff... Make fun of my name again. Go on. I dare you."],["","Ah... I haven't been punched like that in a long time..."],["Refugee B","You... you bastard! Don't you know how much Skysweep has helped us out here in Sankara?"],["Refugee B","If it weren't for him smuggling food and supplies over, who knows how many people would be starving right now? What good are you Vesper compared to him?"],["Arthur","This punch has nothing to do with Vesper, it's personal... Besides, hasn't Vesper been working hard to keep you supplied?"],["Refugee B","Hah, you're proud of that meager support?"],["Arthur","Damn it... So you would rather side with this grain-trafficking merchant than believe in Vesper, who've always helped you for free...?"],["Skysweep","Cough, cough... I told you, little girl, the more you explain, the worse the situation will get."],["Skysweep","Sigh, that's a hell of a punch you've got. Why are all the women I meet so damn tough...?"],["","Skysweep wobbles up from the ground. He wipes the blood from the corner of his mouth with the back of his hand, still wearing that cynical smile."],["Skysweep","Since you want to improve the lives of the Milkhamans, why not buy fewer STs and use the extra money to help Sankara?"],["Arthur","Well, you see..."],["Skysweep","Wait, let me guess... You're protecting the mining area, right? Stop with the lame excuses..."],["Skysweep","We told you earlier, the DL didn't dare to mess with the mining area much before you came. It was only after you arrived that all this nonsense started. Cause and effect, yeah? You've got them reversed!"],["Skysweep","From my perspective as a fourth party, it's precisely because of your armed force that so many conflicts have arisen... Seriously, what's the point of having all your resources if you don't improve the lives of ordinary people?"],["Refugee A","I... I think Skysweep makes a good point..."],["Refugee B","Exactly, exactly. You guys are well-fed and full of ideals. Meanwhile we're still hungry!"],["Arthur","You... you..."],["","Arthur furrows her brow, scanning the surroundings. At this moment, she can't see everyone's faces clearly, only feeling that everything around her is an enemy."],["","Just like at the orphanage, you need to fight against the whole world to earn the right to survive."],["Skysweep","Enough talk. Maybe you should let everyone meet your sponsors. Let's skip the middlemen and let the Milkhamans decide for themselves."],["Skysweep","Keep it up, everyone! We can't let these guys have their way, or things will only get harder down the road!"],["","The discontent among the crowd grows louder. The Vesper soldiers struggling to maintain order begin to falter. Arthur's unease intensifies as she spots Skysweep trying to slip away once again."],["","What should she do now? Should she attempt to calm the crowd, or should she capture this suspicious character for interrogation?"],["","If he really poses no threat and is just a simple grain merchant, that'll surely make things worse..."],["Cassha","Arthur, I'm up to speed. Lorenzo will handle the situation on site. Don't let that guy get away."],["Arthur","...I understand, Miss Cassha."],["","Fortunately, this was something more suitable for her skillset."]],"468257301":[["Arthur","Judging by the way you handle yourself, you're no mere passerby... Be honest, who sent you?"],["Skysweep","Sigh... Seems I should have surrendered from the start to avoid all this trouble."],["Arthur","It won't be long before that smile is wiped off your face."],["Cassha","Seems I arrived just in time... Well done, Arthur."],["","An ST stops not far away, and Cassha joins the interrogation. For some reason, Arthur feels relieved."],["","This Skysweep likes to ask tricky questions. Rather than answering, she prefers to solve problems through combat."],["Arthur","Cassha, who exactly is this guy...?"],["Cassha","Stephen Butler, codename Skysweep, a member of the Thunderbolt Squad... Do you remember the lab we were preparing to raid a month ago, but someone else looted it first?"],["Arthur","...The Thunderbolt Squad did it?"],["Skysweep","...Oh? Are we that famous?"],["","Skysweep shrugs, clearly unconcerned about his identity being exposed."],["Cassha","Vesper has been tracking your whereabouts. Ever since that attack, the squad vanished completely—even you, who often frequents the black markets of various factions."],["Skysweep","Well, we did cause quite a stir back then. Naturally, we had to lay low. As for why I'm showing up now? It's simple, people need to eat. If I don't come out to grab some supplies, the squad won't be able to keep going..."],["Cassha","Spare me the excuses, Skysweep. I want to ask if you're willing to assist Vesper. We should be united in our goal against the DL..."],["Skysweep","I speak for the whole team, except for those two crazy ladies. The answer's no."],["Skysweep","We do enjoy causing some trouble, but we don't want to die like fools, understand?"],["Arthur","Are you saying we can't handle the upcoming attack? Cassha, let's not waste time with this guy..."],["Skysweep","Uh... Miss Arthur, seems you missed my point. We don't want to die \"like fools.\""],["Skysweep","When you were arguing with those Milkhamans, didn't you realize? You're fighting for a bunch of people who don't even want independence. You'd die for that?"],["Cassha","It's just a few agitators confusing the public—just like what you were doing earlier."],["Skysweep","Oh? Is that really the case?"],["Skysweep","I never expected this, Cassha Lumiere. You experienced the Milkhama War firsthand—how could you not get it either?"],["Skysweep","For civilians, it's always the ones in the rear who shout loudest about winning everything back through war—because the shells never fall on their heads."],["Skysweep","Those suckers on the front lines, after being rattled by shells a few times, quickly become the most genuine pacifists."],["Skysweep","Even if that peace is bought with their submission, they still see it as more than worthwhile."],["Arthur","Cassha..."],["Cassha","...I understand what you mean. Now I have another question: why did you risk appearing in this place?"],["","Skysweep's words indeed reveal certain truths. With the DLAF piling on the pressure, the shift in Free Milkhama's attitude towards Vesper has been clear as day."],["","Unlike Arthur, Cassha maintains a calm expression throughout. She raises her rifle and aims it at her opponent's head."],["Cassha","And I still need a reason not to execute a desperado like you on the spot."],["Skysweep","As for why I appeared... it was to have this conversation with you, to give you a heads-up, so you wouldn't die clueless."],["Arthur","What do you mean..."],["Mirestomp","Skysweep, lower your head."],["Skysweep","Alright!"],["Cassha","Arthur, get down!"],["","*boom*"],["","Beside them, a garrisoned Vesper ST suddenly activates. Cassha tackles the stunned Arthur to the ground, dodging a series of bullets from the spray."],["","The ST quickly moves to Skysweep's side, opening its cockpit to let him in."],["","Cassha and the pilot make eye contact."],["Mirestomp","So you're still using the same encryption and piloting system... It's been a long time, Captain Cassha."],["Cassha","Snow Kratt... So you're still alive."],["Mirestomp","You sound disappointed."],["Cassha","...No, the fact that you're still alive is the most important thing."],["Mirestomp","Heh, you're still so considerate... Just to be clear, I've never felt any resentment over that matter."],["Mirestomp","Just looking at the current situation... sigh, Vesper really arrived too early. It's not the right time yet."],["Mirestomp","Keep a closer eye on those you're trying to save. As for whether they're worth the effort, that's for you to decide."],["","The camp is in a shambles after the battle, and the Milkhamans who had gathered there earlier are nowhere to be seen."],["","But soon, they will gather here again, and by then, they will have more evidence to drive these rebels out of their community."],["","The three people who can prevent this situation are currently discussing countermeasures in the operations room."],["Cassha","Two civilian-modified ST units, food and water for fifty people, and basic medical supplies... For now, this is all we can spare."],["Lorenzo","Understood, I'll take care of it."],["","Lorenzo nods to Cassha and pushes the door open. They are running out of time."],["","Cassha lowers her head and continues to ponder. Her face shows no sign of anxiety, which inadvertently puts more pressure on Arthur, who is at a total loss."],["","The troubles vented by punching Skysweep do not take long to make a reappearance."],["Arthur","Sorry, Cassha, it's all because I lost my temper..."],["Cassha","Arthur, what do you think about what those two said?"],["","Cassha doesn't mind Arthur's annoyance. Instead, she poses a question to her."],["Arthur","Those two... Skysweep and Mirestomp? They think we can't possibly hold off the DLAF's attack..."],["Arthur","But they don't know. We don't need to repel them entirely—we just need to buy enough time."],["Cassha","All this nonsense isn't worth the risk for them."],["Cassha","I don't know the reason, but in their roundabout way, I think the Thunderbolt Squad is trying to help us."],["","Suddenly, Cassha seems to realize something and turns her gaze to the battle map on the table, drawing two circles on it with the pen beside her."],["Arthur","These two places are... the internal areas of Sankara? Cassha, didn't you say that due to public opinion and Tiphys's influence, the DLAF couldn't easily break in?"],["Cassha","Arthur, prepare a squad. We need to split up and investigate these two areas."],["Cassha","It's not about checking the movements of the DLAF or Obsidian, but rather, as they said... focusing on those we fight for."]],"468261101":[["","Chapter 2"],["","Sankara Analysis Room"],["","In the empty analysis room, a group of guards lay sprawled. Their bodies formed a path leading all the way to a frail figure standing in front of a computer."],["???","I've made it..."],["","The girl types briskly on the keyboard, her eyes darting between reports and data, searching for her objective."],["Ma'at","Well done, Vera."],["Ma'at","Afterward, you just need to send me over a copy of the file for Victoria, and we'll make arrangements for your withdrawal."],["Vera","That won't be necessary."],["","Vera ends the call. She stops briefly, tilts her head, and listens intently to the silence in the analysis room after the keyboard sounds cease."],["Cassha","...Have I been discovered?"],["","Cassha emerges from behind the wall dozens of meters away. Though silent, the girl still senses her presence."],["Cassha","Which faction are you from? Such perception is rare here on Milkhama... anywhere in fact."],["Vera","No, no... it's just that the entire analysis room is equipped with life detection sensors."],["Vera","While I was still wondering if there was an issue with the instrument, you appeared before me."],["","Vera has no intention of bluffing. She openly admits her methods to the enemy in front of her."],["Cassha","But from another perspective, no one can sneak into this analysis room, right?"],["","Cassha has no choice but to move closer to Vera, maintaining an ambiguous distance that allows her to guard against Vera's sudden attack and anticipate her next move."],["","Including the ST standing beside her."],["Vera","Perhaps... After all, this is one of the most tightly guarded places in Sankara. The mining conditions of all the mines, the deployment of troops, and even the lands temporarily handed over to Vesper are all well documented."],["Cassha","Then I definitely can't let you go... But before that, can you tell me how you got here?"],["Vera","Are you trying to stall for time and gather more troops to restrain me?"],["","Hearing Vera's words, Cassha pauses for a moment before continuing to tap the comms device hidden behind her back, calling guards to her location."],["Vera","But now that you're guarding the door, it's not so easy for me to get out. Talking won't make much difference... Easy to enter, hard to leave. Is this some kind of wonderland in a rabbit hole?"],["Cassha","That's not right. You yourself said that breaking in here is no easy task."],["Vera","For outsiders, that's true. But for a Milkhaman registered in Sankara, it's not difficult at all."],["","Vera no longer seems to see Cassha as a threat. She turns around and continues typing on the keyboard, ignoring her."],["Vera","The automatically triggered alarms are useless. Once here, all I need to do is take anyone down who tries to pull the manual alarm."],["Cassha","In other words, you're a traitor to Sankara, right?"],["Vera","A traitor... Is that what I am?"],["","Cassha's accusations don't affect Vera in the slightest. It seems that in her eyes, \"traitor\" is not a derogatory term."],["Cassha","You know perfectly well. The DL's interference in Sankara is deepening day by day. The so-called Milkhaman Autonomous Region exists now in name only. For you, as a Milkhaman, to do such a thing..."],["Vera","What does this have to do with me?"],["Cassha","...!?"],["Vera","It seems you misunderstand the concept of \"traitor.\""],["Vera","A traitor is someone who betrays the one they are loyal to, right? And the one worth our loyalty should be the one who has provided us with shelter and protection, shouldn't it?"],["Vera","In other words, the relationship of loyalty is actually a cooperative relationship."],["Vera","But my mother and I have never received any care or protection from Sankara... not even once..."],["Vera","So my actions can't really be considered betrayal, can they?"],["","Vera sighs and turns to Cassha, whose gun is silently aimed at her head."],["","It seems no one wants to listen to a \"traitor\" and their long-winded speech."],["Vera","Cassha Lumiere, have you ever considered whether Sankara is truly worth sacrificing everything for?"],["Cassha","Spare me the outdated rhetoric. If there were still doubts, our team wouldn't have made it this far."],["Vera","But you know what? The people here are no longer the same as when you left."],["Cassha","Oh? That's impressive. You've investigated my past?"],["","Bang!"],["","In the midst of the conversation, Cassha suddenly opens fire, leaving only a crisp clanging sound. It is Vera's ST that extends its hand to block the shot for her."],["","Her ST is also equipped with the PAMS system, allowing it to autonomously react even without a pilot."],["Vera","After the Milkhama War ended, you left Milkhama Island and embarked on a journey that lasted several decades, returning only two years ago."],["Vera","The era when Milkhamans stood united against a common enemy is long gone—you just refuse to admit it."],["Cassha","Of course I understand. But just like the great war back then, someone has to act—to awaken their will."],["Vera","And you think they'll be grateful? Hah. Don't make me laugh..."],["","Cassha frowns. She understands that everything the girl says is true—at least, true from her point of view."],["","Unfortunate truths."],["Vera","The people here always wear the mask of victims—constantly demanding from others, never knowing satisfaction or gratitude... like animals that can never be tamed."],["Vera","No—worse than animals. They even feel jealousy, that uniquely human kind of ugliness."],["Vera","The moment one of them gets a chance to escape their fate, the rest claw them back like crabs in a bucket."],["Vera","Hahaha, isn't it funny? Unlike the renaissance period when you left, these guys are clearly suffering, but they spend all day scheming against each other, afraid that someone around them might escape first!"],["Vera","Mom just doesn't understand this. They dragged her down. Otherwise, I could've gotten her out..."],["Cassha","Alright, you don't need to say anymore."],["","One Vesper ST after another arrives in the analysis room, muzzles trained on Vera and her rig. The girl's words spiral out of control, and any chance of escape disappears."],["Cassha","Everything you said, I also experienced in that war. It's an undeniable fact..."],["Vera","Then why are you unwilling to admit it? Your efforts and sacrifices now will only become a joke in the mouths of those guys later! They're worthless!"],["Cassha","Because after that, I witnessed something different: hope."],["Cassha","It also made me realize that true hope will not be buried by everything you mentioned. In the end, it will reveal itself to the world."],["Cassha","This is a fact you either don't know or are as yet unwilling to see."]],"468261301":[["","The battle was one-sided."],["","Cassha's squad subdue Vera. She is dragged from her ST, her indifferent expression gone, replaced with a tinge of hatred."],["Cassha","Those documents you stole... Who gave the orders?"],["Vera","Hmph..."],["","Vera turns her head aside. It's obvious that no one is getting anything out of her anytime soon."],["Cassha","Take her away, then clean up the scene. I'll explain everything to Free Milkhama later..."],["","Alert! Breach in the Analysis Room detected!"],["Cassha","So that's how it is... Well, Arthur can handle it on her own..."],["","As the alarm blares, a large number of refugee STs pour in, surrounding Cassha and her team."],["Refugee","This is Sankara's Intelligence Analysis Room. How did you guys... What?"],["Cassha","We are Vesper. We discovered hostile intruders at this location. You just missed the capture operation."],["","Cassha gives a signal and the STs stand down, relaxing their combat-ready state. She steps forward. Her mind races with a flurry of strategies, each capable of breaking through the blockade with ease, but she dismisses them one by one."],["","Any aggressive action would only exacerbate the distrust between them and Sankara, which is something they want to avoid at all costs."],["","So her choice is to raise her hands, giving up any resistance."],["Refugee","What a joke, we haven't seen any intruders except you guys..."],["Vera","Enough talk... No matter the truth, they'll find a way to blame it all on you!"],["Vera","You're still wasting time on them, even in this situation? These useless people? They'll only hold you back..."],["Cassha","Vera, you mentioned earlier that the era of that rebellion war is over, right?"],["","Without turning around or raising her voice, Cassha cuts off Vera's mockery with calm ease."],["","Why? Even as she surrenders, Vera senses no hesitation from Cassha, only determination."],["","As if... in the end, she was right."],["Cassha","But have you ever wondered why that era came to be?"],["Vera","..."],["","Faced with the approaching refugees, one by one, the Vesper soldiers with Cassha dismount their STs in surrender."],["","Vera feels an unbearable frustration. These hypocritical rebels do not tear off their masks as she expects—instead, they face the ignorant masses in a way she finds completely baffling."],["","Absurd... But how did these fools manage to get this far...?"],["Cassha","Everyone knows that on September 17, 1995, Ben McCarthy led over fifty workers to break through the Obsidian blockade, launching a remarkable armed labor uprising. Yet this was preceded by six even larger uprisings."],["Cassha","These rebellions all failed without exception. More than half of them were crushed in the cradle by Obsidian due to betrayal by other laborers."],["Vera","This..."],["Cassha","I remember once, while rummaging through a trash can in an alley for food, I happened to see my uncle bowing and scraping before an Obsidian employee... That night, Obsidian's people broke into the home of a rebel leader, leaving behind only blood and carnage."],["Cassha","Rebellion can never succeed, that's what everyone thinks... But what I remember more deeply is that person who once raised their arm and shouted at a labor meeting..."],["Cassha","\"This is not the sign of our defeat—it is the promise that our struggle will outlive us all!\""],["Cassha","And indeed, as he shouted... The crueler the suppression, the fiercer the rebellion. Countless people bled, countless people sacrificed, and countless more joined them on that path..."],["Cassha","Not because those people were foolish, but because, apart from death, the Milkhamans had nothing else... Just a little spark is needed to ignite the firewood of rebellion."],["Cassha","The betrayal, numbness, and tragic futile resistance you now despise are merely stages on the path to struggle. And we are merely the keepers of the kindling."],["Vera","..."],["Vera","No... just some pretty words..."],["","Refugees begin restraining Vesper soldiers. Vera's voice starts to tremble. She buries her head between her knees, no longer looking at Cassha's back."],["Vera","The dead went away without considering what those left behind should do."],["Vera","Right now, you're no different from Mother, just being bled dry and discarded by these guys..."],["Cassha","She must have been a wonderful mother, right?"],["Vera","...No, she was so naive, too naive to see through those bastards' intentions."],["Vera","Still believing in the ideal of Milkhamans helping each other, working together to build a home..."],["Cassha","But do you blame her for that?"],["Vera","..."],["Cassha","In a way, we're no different from the mother you speak of, firmly believing in some rather naive ideals as our principle for survival."],["Cassha","Perhaps our fate will be as tragic as you say, unable to achieve victory... but in return, we have also planted the seeds of hope."],["Cassha","Vesper will awaken the will to resist, leading more to join this wave and march toward ultimate victory."],["Cassha","And your mother, she left you."],["Cassha","And I'm sure that someone like her would be proud of you no matter what."],["Vera","...!!!"],["","Vera suddenly raises her head, and in a daze, Cassha's back seems to transform into that frail figure in the dim light, worrying about her next tuition fee."],["","She once promised to take her away from here, to find true happiness, but all she got were bitter smiles. It made her angry."],["","\"Don't worry about how Mom is doing, just take care of yourself.\""],["","Those evasive answers made Vera lose her temper again and again, but... but..."],["","Does she really want to blame her?"],["Cassha","Don't let hatred blind your eyes. Cherish the hope your mother left behind..."],["Cassha","You're not a bad kid."],["Vera","You...?"],["","The refugee interrupts Cassha, grabs her hands, and roughly pushes her forward."],["Vera","Wait..."],["","Vera stands up firmly and calls out to Cassha and the refugee escorting her."],["","Her eyes no longer dodge, revealing an unspoken determination."],["Vera","I am the intruder, and I will explain to you all that happened."],["Cassha","That's a great help..."],["Vera","Don't get me wrong, I don't think you're right, nor do I think your ideals can be realized..."],["Vera","I just... don't want you to end up like my mom."]],"468269101":[["","Chapter 3"],["Arthur","Here are coordinates Cassha gave us..."],["","Before arriving here, the anxious Arthur imagined many scenarios. Perhaps a large number of Vesper's dissenters were waiting for mediation, or some unknown enemy lurking in the shadows... Frankly speaking, she preferred the latter."],["","But upon reaching this small town, Arthur's doubts reach their peak, as though turning into something tangible, shrouding her vision."],["","It isn't that she sees enemies or evidence of danger—it's that... there is nothing here at all."],["","This small town is completely deserted."],["Arthur","Something's off. The map was just updated three days ago. I remember the residents here refused to withdraw, and since it's a necessary passage for the <yellow>DLAF's advance</yellow>, it was eventually handed over to Sankara as one of their self-defense areas."],["","Arthur pilots her ST through the streets. Everything looks normal—no rubble, no blood, no scorch marks. The town stands intact, except for one thing: the Milkhamans are gone."],["","Even the soil of the makeshift road appears undisturbed. Besides two refugee transport trucks parked by the roadside, there are not many <yellow>traces of STs or other vehicles coming through</yellow>."],["","She suddenly misses the Milkhamans, even if their \"warm greetings\" usually mean hurling garbage and other unmentionables at them. Far from pleasant, it is still preferable to the eerie vibe this place gives off."],["","This is new. Something is wrong."],["Arthur","I should report what happened here to Cassha..."],["","Arthur dials Cassha's private number, but for some reason, the channel that usually connects instantly only offers an anxiety-inducing busy tone in reply."],["","For now, she is alone."],["Arthur","..."],["","Her ST's cockpit opens, and Arthur leaps down, scanning the surroundings cautiously before entering a nearby residence."],["Arthur","Anyone home?"],["","She is faced with a large dormitory converted from a factory—not uncommon in Sankara, a mining town."],["","Without the greatest confidence, Arthur calls out. After hearing only echoes in response, she ventures further in."],["Arthur","Strange, where did everyone go...?"],["","At the back, a makeshift kitchen, steam rising from the <yellow>still-hot soup</yellow>... Arthur's questions begin to multiply."],["","A dining table. On top, a flyer catches her attention."],["Arthur","This is..."],["Flyer","To prepare for the upcoming battle against the DL, Vesper will occupy this town as a defensive stronghold. Former Sankara residents are advised to evacuate immediately or face severe consequences."],["Arthur","What's going on?! There's no way Vesper would send such a message. This must be..."],["","Arthur flips through the flyer, trying to find a clue."],["","This is definitely a product of <yellow>rushed printing</yellow>. It hasn't been long, yet the words have already faded somewhat. The low-quality paper crumbles and cracks between her fingers."],["Arthur","Who could've forged something like this...?"],["Vesper Soldier","Report, forged Vesper declarations have been found in the surrounding residences!"],["","So, did the residents here evacuate because of this false information?"],["","No, it doesn't seem that simple... If it's the Sankara residents I know..."],["Vesper Soldier","Captain, there's an ST signal coming from the northwest!"],["","A new report interrupts Arthur's thoughts. Without reaching an understanding of just what is going on, a fresh problem presents itself."],["","As indicated by her companion, several STs outside town are slowly approaching."],["","As the distance closes, the STs are confirmed as belonging to Free Milkhama. They lower their guard."],["Vesper Soldier","What the... Aren't those guys Free Milkhama?"],["Arthur","No... Stay alert."],["","Arthur still feels uneasy about pointing guns at Milkhamans."],["","Indeed, despite her conflicts with the local residents, she never intended to use violence. She'd let her anger out on her weapons, tinkering with them into the night."],["","Protecting the Milkhamans has always been Vesper's ultimate goal, and empowering them to fight for themselves is the best and only viable means to achieve it."],["","God helps those who help themselves. They have to understand."],["","So although Arthur issues the order to stay alert, they are only to stay on guard—not to open fire."],["","This will prove to be a mistake borne out of rigid adherence to principle."],["???","Vesper's people? Isn't this <yellow>too soon</yellow>?"],["","The opposing ST comes to a slow halt before them. Its pilot dismounts and walks straight up to Arthur, completely unguarded."],["","Facing several fully armed STs, he shows no fear or tension at all. A true veteran."],["Arthur","Who are you? Why are you here?"],["Vesper Soldier","Is that... Aiden?"],["Vesper Soldier","Captain, if I remember correctly, he's a member of the Free Milkhama Defense Force, a merc who landed on the island during the war."],["Vesper Soldier","Before we arrived, they took on peacekeeping work for Free Milkhama and even had several skirmishes with the DLAF."],["Aiden","Oh, am I that famous?"],["Aiden","That's right, I'm Aiden Grimwald, the one in charge of guarding this area. I've been waiting for you."],["","Aiden waves cheerfully at the surrounding STs, easing the tension in the air."],["Aiden","Hey, girl, are you that... Arthur? We've heard quite a bit about you here. You've been causing the DLAF some trouble, huh?"],["Arthur","..."],["Arthur","What's going on here? Where have all the residents gone?"],["Aiden","Did you see that flyer?"],["Arthur","..."],["","The suspicious flyer. That forged Vesper declaration."],["Aiden","Not long ago, it was delivered to every household, causing widespread panic. We decided to relocate the residents to other towns and contact Vesper to verify whether it was real."],["Arthur","It's fake. Vesper would never force Sankara residents to evacuate."],["Aiden","Oh really...? Can you really guarantee that no Vesper would ever do such a thing?"],["Arthur","Of course! Vesper's goal is liberation, why would they..."],["","Although Arthur reacts quickly and intensely, her tone lacks absolute confidence."],["","She can speak for herself and Cassha—they would never abuse the rights of those they seek to protect. But the others...?"],["","It's the devil's proof. How does one prove a negative? Difficult, if not impossible."],["","Seeing Arthur's somewhat grim expression, Aiden laughs and waves his hand."],["Aiden","Haha, I'm not trying to corner you. It's just that when any organization reaches a certain level of development, these kinds of things are inevitable, right?"],["Aiden","Unity is something you can only boast about when you're still a small group. Once the organization grows to the point where not everyone recognizes everyone else, no one can make any guarantees."],["Aiden","Whether it's Sankara or Vesper, it's all the same."],["","No, the reality is even more severe than Aiden suggests. You can't even fully guarantee those closest to you—otherwise, you fall into an endless loop of self-justification."],["","The tragedies caused by proving loyalty are stories heard a thousand times."],["","But now's not the time to dwell on such things. The important matter is the issue at hand."],["Arthur","If you think Vesper's behind all this trouble, then what's the point of discussing it with us?"],["Aiden","I trust that you core members will stick to your principles, so I hope you can investigate the nearby Vesper garrison. Is that alright?"],["","Diplomatically, Aiden doesn't clash with Arthur and the others, instead leaving them a chance to prove their innocence."],["","Compared to the more radical Milkhamans, this is restraint."],["","An eminently reasonable offer, with little reason to turn it down..."],["Arthur","I refuse."],["Aiden","We'll continue to guard this town to ensure... What?"],["Arthur","The instructions I received were not to investigate issues related to Vesper, but rather the issues in this area."],["Arthur","You can make a formal application to headquarters. Cassha will definitely send someone else over soon..."],["Aiden","But as you can see, the issues here have already been clarified. There's nothing to investigate."],["Aiden","Or are you saying... you just don't trust Milkhamans?"],["","With Arthur's rejection, the originally harmonious atmosphere turns icy."],["Arthur","No... Even though many Milkhamans don't welcome us or trust us, I still believe that the Milkhamans will eventually move in the right direction."],["Arthur","Because I believe. And that belief in the Milkhamans means I cannot overlook what's happening here."],["Arthur","Even if it makes us more unpopular for the time being, I have to do what I have to do."],["","If it were Cassha or Lorenzo, they would surely come up with a better solution, but Arthur struggles."],["","She only does what she wants to do in the moment, regardless of the outcome."],["Aiden","You're stubborn... But were it not for that, you wouldn't be standing here now, would you?"],["Aiden","Come on, what are those contradictions you mentioned? Point them out, and I'll help you resolve them."],["Arthur","Thank you... So the first point is, when exactly did the refugees evacuate this town?"],["Aiden","It was roughly around dawn, today. When everyone woke up, they found the declaration had been posted to their homes, causing panic, and then..."],["Arthur","No, something's wrong... If they withdrew at that time, it would have been about six hours ago. The residential area wouldn't be like this."],["","Arthur points out the hot soup. Judging by the temperature, they left only one or two hours ago at most."],["Aiden","Maybe they forgot to turn off the stove when they left... Haha, I remember now, that family didn't see the declaration and missed the main retreat, so we specifically went to pick them up later."],["","So amidst the widespread panic, they somehow failed to notice what was happening and continued preparing lunch...?"],["","I mean, that is indeed possible, but it also raises other questions..."],["Arthur","How did those supposed \"Vesper\" manage to deliver flyers to everyone without anyone noticing?"],["Aiden","I'm afraid I don't know. As for their criminal methods, that's something for you to investigate."],["Arthur","Right... but how did the residents leave the town?"],["Aiden","Transport trucks. Each town has a few lying around to handle emergency evacuations."],["Arthur","Just those?"],["","Arthur points to the transport trucks parked by the roadside not far away and asks."],["Aiden","Ah, that's right. After dropping people off, we drove them back. If a battle does break out, they'll be used again to transport supplies or to aid a retreat, and so on."],["","Aiden quickly answers Arthur's questions, but something crucial appears to have slipped by him..."],["Arthur","But after an evacuation on that scale, there'd be tracks all over the roads!"],["Arthur","From what I can see, there are signs of at most a single ST squad coming through—certainly not a town-sized refugee convoy!"],["Aiden","Well, you see, the town only has a small population. We didn't need that many..."],["Arthur","Hmm... Then why prepare all these vehicles?"],["","Aiden is grasping at straws. His smile stiffens as Arthur closes in on the truth."],["Aiden","Why? I don't know. Maybe they're for people who'll move in later. It's all decided by higher-ups."],["Arthur","Aiden, what exactly are you hiding...?"],["Aiden","I'm not hiding anything from you. These are the facts."],["Arthur","Then how do you explain the most important point? As a Milkhaman, you should understand it better than I do..."],["","Arthur takes a deep breath and utters the point that has puzzled her from the beginning."],["","Even as a native of the DL, through the events of these last few years, she has come to grasp this truth—a truth that has stirred her soul."],["Arthur","If they really did receive this declaration—Milkhamans don't run so easily."],["Aiden","..."],["Arthur","Especially these Milkhamans who decided to guard the area themselves. For them it's not about words and feelings; they're willing to fight with their own hands to protect their land."],["Arthur","How could these proud people simply roll over in the face of a mere piece of paper?"],["","Arthur speaks, taking a step forward, and looks directly into Aiden's somewhat wavering eyes."],["","Her claim, without evidence, based on pure conviction—this is the decisive proof."],["Arthur","I believe in the Milkhamans!"],["","Her voice is loud and powerful, like a sharp blade cutting through the solitude of this deserted town."],["Arthur","It doesn't matter if they don't trust Vesper. What matters is that these are the homes they built themselves, and they see them as theirs to defend!"],["Arthur","As long as they maintain the spirit of resistance, then our actions have not been in vain! They have meaning!"],["Arthur","At least, that's what I believe... Cassha and everyone in Vesper believe it too!"],["","It is as if she isn't speaking to Aiden, but making an announcement to the entire town."],["","This is the true message of Vesper."],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","Hahaha... This is bad..."],["","Watching Arthur, whose face is flushed and who is slightly breathless from excitement, Aiden suddenly covers his face and starts laughing."],["","When his laughter ends, his tone is no longer tensely pretentious. Instead, he sounds relieved."],["Aiden","So what do you think the truth is? After saying so much, you must have had an idea from the very beginning, right?"],["Arthur","..."],["Arthur","I can't believe someone would do such a thing. It's despicable..."],["Aiden","I never thought an outsider would make a deduction based on \"trusting the Milkhamans\"... It'd be a shame if you didn't reveal your reasoning."],["","Arthur takes two steps back. She trusts the Milkhamans, and if her guess is correct, the man in front of her has also designed a scheme based on \"trusting the Milkhamans.\""],["","It is a chilling plan, and whether she explains her reasoning or not, a price must be paid for what has happened."],["","But facing such a trap, this is something only Arthur can do."],["Arthur","Aiden, you are the one who forged the declaration, aren't you?"],["Aiden","..."],["","Before Aiden even replies, a heavy machine gun in the hands of his companion's ST begins spinning into readiness."],["Arthur","!!!"],["","The bullets come faster than Arthur's orders. Vesper soldiers are caught in the spray before they can respond—but they still manage one thing..."],["","Using his body to shield Arthur from a round of bullets, a Vesper soldier gives Arthur an opening to attack."],["Aiden","Arthur, maybe you're right..."],["Aiden","But Sankara can't afford another failure."]],"468269301":[["Arthur","Don't think you can escape that easily..."],["","Arthur swings the cockpit door wide. Aiden sits slumped in the breached ST, the will to fight gone, answering her fury with only a faint, defiant smile."],["Arthur","I'm not finished!"],["Aiden","Cough, cough... Is this what you want? To make me to listen to some long-winded speech...?"],["Arthur","No... I know the \"how\" but not the \"why.\" What's your motive?"],["Arthur","That answer can only come from you, a Milkhaman."],["Aiden","A Milkhaman? That's not quite right. I'm not one of them—just a mercenary with nowhere to go after the war."],["Arthur","But they trust you more than Vesper, don't they?"],["Arthur","That's why they believed you."],["Aiden","..."],["Arthur","I've been thinking about how the declaration could be delivered to everyone without detection... It seems only you, as the defense force, had the means, right?"],["Arthur","\"We received a bunch of Vesper's flyers just now, and now we're distributing them to inform everyone of the situation...\" This would make sure everyone receives the message and can start getting ready..."],["Aiden","What's the point of spreading such rumors in this remote town...?"],["Arthur","This gives you a suitable reason to send the residents away, such as \"to fight Vesper to the end for disturbing the residents' daily lives,\" which is what they want..."],["Aiden","This kind of battle is utterly meaningless..."],["","Aiden's lips tremble slightly as he murmurs, his voice so low that only he can hear it."],["Arthur","But battle was never your goal—it was merely a promise you made in response to the residents."],["Aiden","..."],["Arthur","So at the very beginning, you only suggested I investigate the nearby Vesper outpost instead of launching a surprise attack."],["Aiden","Heh, what's the point of all this? The truth will come out sooner or later..."],["Arthur","I've already said, sending the residents away was your goal in itself."],["Arthur","After that, it no longer mattered if things were exposed; no direct loss had been caused.. People will just see it as more baseless provocation."],["Arthur","You even went so far as to call in Vesper's own people to look into it, all in the hope that your self-scripted play would close flawlessly. But fate sent us instead—never part of the plan—and that's why you blurted out that remark about it being \"too soon.\""],["Aiden","..."],["Arthur","But fortunately, we still made it in time, didn't we? As long as those people can pass through this town without being noticed by the residents."],["Vesper Soldier","Captain Arthur, who are those people you're referring to...?"],["Arthur","It can only be the DLAF."],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","You're right, if they discover DLAF troops approaching, a battle will be inevitable..."],["","Rather than an explanation, Aiden's words sound more like a helpless sigh."],["Arthur","..."],["Arthur","Let's go. If we catch up now, it should still be in time."],["","Arthur doesn't continue to press Aiden, a defeated man. And she has more important things to do."],["","A new obstacle appears before them."],["Refugee","Vesper scum! Get out! Now!"],["Vesper Soldier","Weren't these people already relocated elsewhere?"],["","One by one, residents begin to appear on the streets, surrounding Arthur's troops. They wield various homemade weapons, using their bodies to block these cold steel giants."],["","Unlike the protests in other areas, the residents here are silent. Their actions are the most effective form of resistance."],["Arthur","The disappearance occurred in less than an hour, without using any transportation. The residents of this town did not relocate to other areas as Aiden suggested, but instead relied on years of experience resisting their oppressors to hide in place."],["Arthur","Even if we expose Aiden's conspiracy, there's nothing we can do. The theory is just conjecture. There's no hard proof."],["Arthur","And if any action is taken, the blame will fall completely on Vesper..."],["","Perhaps leaving as per Aiden's suggestion would have been a better choice, avoiding this inevitable defeat."],["","But Arthur still went ahead, a decision only she could make."],["Vesper Soldier","So... Captain, what should we do...?"],["Arthur","I don't know... Aiden, to go this far..."],["Aiden","If you surrender quietly, I will testify later that this was just a misunderstanding."],["Arthur","No, what I want to know is why you, who tried so hard to avoid conflict and even used the residents as leverage, ultimately chose to use battle to buy time."],["Arthur","If someone dies in this pointless battle, who will bear the responsibility for this meaningless bloodshed?"],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","I'm not afraid of bleeding. What I fear is... the bleeding of others."],["Aiden","If my sacrifice can bring about peace and prevent the impending war, then so be it."],["Aiden","Even if it means betraying everyone."],["","Aiden stands up, gasping for breath. His eyes gaze past Arthur, past the townspeople below, and toward the distant horizon. He speaks softly, whispering words only Arthur can hear."],["Aiden","As long as we can assist the DL forces in completing this raid, Vesper will collapse without a fight, and everything will return to the way it was."],["Arthur","..."],["Aiden","Arthur, I know your background."],["Aiden","A DL orphan taken in by Vesper. Always surrounded by those who yearn for rebellion and struggle. But have you ever thought about what the ordinary people of Sankara want?"],["Arthur","You self-righteous son-of-a..."],["Aiden","Unlike you, they still have families. They still have people they're willing to give their lives for, people they want to protect... and in war, all of that will—"],["Arthur","You're really... pissing me off!"],["","Arthur cuts off Aiden's rambling. She strides forward, leaps down from the ST, her body tracing a clean arc through the air before landing squarely in front of him."],["","Amid the residents' gasps, Arthur lifts her head, eyes blazing. She grabs Aiden by the collar, yanking him back from that hollow distance, forcing him to meet her gaze."],["Arthur","Hey! How long do you plan to keep prattling on?"],["Arthur","If you're like the others, opposing us, thinking we're the bad guys, I've seen plenty of that... I don't care..."],["Arthur","But, you bastard, what gives you the right to act all high and mighty, making decisions for everyone?"],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","I just chose the facts, something only we who have experienced failure can..."],["","*smack!*"],["","The sharp slap cuts him off completely."],["Arthur","...Look at these people, and then think about how ridiculous your words are."],["","Under Arthur's pressure, Aiden is forced to look at the residents. Doubt finally creeps across his face."],["","Before, when he glanced at them, it wasn't indifference—it was avoidance."],["Arthur","They want to fight. They want to give themselves for their home, for their people. And your deception strips them of that choice."],["Aiden","No, it was my plan that made their sacrifice unnecessary!"],["Aiden","You're not even a Milkhaman—what right do you have...?"],["Arthur","Yes, I'm not a Milkhaman. I have no right to meddle in Sankara's internal affairs, nor have I ever thought of doing so."],["Aiden","In that case, you..."],["Arthur","But growing up in a DL orphanage, I was raised listening to people like you."],["Arthur","\"Arthur, you should be more ladylike...\" \"Stop tinkering with machines all day...\" \"Why are you fussing about your name again? It's the last gift your parents left you...\""],["Arthur","They wanted to forge me into the shape they desired, to smile and forgive those who mocked, bullied, and ignored me, in order to gain the right to stay in the DL... But is that what I wanted?"],["Arthur","Then Vesper came into my life. Unlike those adults before, they didn't force us. They gave us a choice."],["Arthur","That choice back then shaped who I am today, a soldier, about to participate in a war with an almost certain chance of defeat."],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","You could've had a better life..."],["Arthur","You're wrong. I'm satisfied with my path—because it's the one I chose."],["Arthur","And what about these Milkhamans?"],["","Arthur releases Aiden and lets out a sigh, not for herself, but for everyone present."],["Arthur","Aiden, your well-intentioned \"deception\" is in fact the worst kind of \"coercion,\" and that is what I cannot accept."],["Arthur","Please... stop hiding the truth. Give these people their right to choose back."],["Aiden","..."],["Aiden","Haha...hahaha..."],["","Even after being struck by Arthur several times, Aiden had barely reacted. Yet now, with a few abrupt laughs, the spark he wore when they first met slowly returns to his face."],["","The laughter pulls at his many wounds, making him wince."],["Arthur","It's funny, is it...?"],["Aiden","You're naive. You haven't a clue about how the real world works. And yet, it brings to mind a certain truth: wasn't that exactly what sparked the resistance back then...?"],["Arthur","Back then... Are you referring to the Milkhama War?"],["Aiden","No, it was after the war, but before Vesper appeared... We failed back then, utterly. I've regretted it ever since."],["Aiden","Yet I wonder... Being led by my past regrets, trying to avert more failure, more loss... Is failure really something the dead must simply accept?"],["Arthur","I don't know what you're brooding over, but if you understand it's wrong, then hurry up..."],["Aiden","Hey, kid, after all this talk, have you figured out what you're going to do next?"],["Arthur","...Honestly, I don't know."],["Arthur","We will never fire at civilians, so there's no way to escape from this encirclement. All we can do now is send a warning to headquarters."],["Aiden","I can clear the way for you. Let's just consider it a misunderstanding. They'll believe me."],["Arthur","Really?"],["Aiden","But I want to know, are you really prepared?"],["Aiden","After all, this world still belongs to those \"adults\" you mentioned, and annoying guys like me are not uncommon in Sankara..."],["Arthur","Whatever."],["Arthur","Before arguing with you, I was also confused, afraid that everything we do might not be accepted by the Milkhamans..."],["Arthur","But now, whether it's resistance, submission, or escape... as long as it's a choice made by the Milkhamans themselves, we will accept it."],["Arthur","What Vesper wants to do is simply show them that the option of resistance still exists. The final choice remains in their own hands."],["Aiden","Got it."],["Aiden","All I can do is wish you good luck."],["Arthur","...Much appreciated."]],"468265101":[["","Chapter Four"],["","DL Meeting Room"],["Ma'at","Please hold on, the governor is in a meeting..."],["","Move!"],["","After an intense argument, there follows a rush of hurried footsteps."],["","Bang!!!"],["","A kick slams into the door. A visitor breaks through Ma'at's obstruction and strides into the conference room."],["","The brutalized door creaks and slowly rebounds under the impact, leaving a scar on the wall where its handle hits."],["???","...Lukmund Erambard!"],["","After surveying the room and finding her target, the visitor walks up and slams the conference table."],["Lukmund","Lieutenant Victoria, I understand your eagerness to head into battle."],["Lukmund","However, the second amendment to the Expulsion Act has not yet passed the committee's review, and as a member of the local forces, you have no valid basis to participate in the battle..."],["Victoria","Didn't I already say? I didn't bring any troops. I landed alone!"],["","Victoria continues to smack the table as she speaks, like a form of physical punctuation."],["","...Or as if she is slapping the fake smile off the face of the person before her."],["Victoria","This is a battle with my personal honor at stake—it has nothing to do with the local troops!"],["","Ma'at finally arrives, appearing at the doorway. She casts an apologetic glance at Lukmund, preparing to step forward and stop the impatient guest."],["","Lukmund just shakes his head slightly, restraining his loyal deputy with a simple gesture."],["","He is adept at seizing every opportunity, and this unexpected situation is no exception."],["Lukmund","Then I think you should be assigned to the East Milkhama Defense Force like Major Matilda, under the command of Rear Admiral Tiphys..."],["Victoria","Hmph... Do you even know what you're talking about?"],["","The pounding on the table stops, and Victoria lets out a sneer."],["Victoria","Tiphys is only thinking about how to calm things down. Even with full control, the most he could achieve would be to restore the island to its status quo."],["Victoria","Just like after the Milthus Eruption, letting a perfect chance for a counterattack slip away, only to sign that mediocre peace treaty...  And now he wants a repeat performance!"],["Lukmund","But it was that victory that made the Rear Admiral a hero in the war, bringing peace to Milkhama."],["Victoria","What use is a hero who cannot bring true victory?"],["","This question plunges the atmosphere of the conference room into a deep freeze, with only Lukmund's lips curling up slightly."],["","It seems that only now does he begin to take a genuine interest in the young lieutenant before him."],["Lukmund","Alright then, if you don't agree with General Tiphys's philosophy and feel you can't talk to him... how about talking to me? I can help you think of some alternative solutions."],["Victoria","There's no need for that. What I need is the temporary acquiescence of the council behind you, and support for a small squad of Antibodies."],["","Seeing an opening in Lukmund's compromise, Victoria doesn't hesitate. She immediately pulls out a map and unrolls it on the table, taking up most of its surface."],["","Such an old-fashioned map is certainly rare in today's military. It's hard to imagine its owner is such a young and reckless woman, but judging from the notes and legends filled on it, this is the analytical method she knows best."],["","More importantly, and easily overlooked, she is just an outsider who arrived on the island two days ago."],["Victoria","Tiphys's tactics can indeed ensure the complete extermination of Vesper, but this also inadvertently gives the opponent time to prepare. Once a tug-of-war officially begins, the defense forces will incur many unnecessary costs."],["Victoria","Don't forget, the NDF is also watching us at this moment... This approach, which does not allow for failure, will only take the DL further away from full victory."],["","Victoria points out several potential hotspots where large-scale conflicts might erupt. Lukmund remembers that this aligns almost perfectly with the internal plan circulating within military command."],["Victoria","But this high-profile approach also creates an excellent opportunity. It is now a de facto truce period, and everyone is waiting for the impending decisive battle."],["","Her hand traces another mark on the map, pointing directly to the heart of Vesper as predicted by the DL."],["Victoria","If I lead a surprise attack to strike at the enemy's nerve center, we can easily pave the way to future victory."],["Lukmund","...This is a gamble. Have you a withdrawal strategy?"],["Victoria","Retreat? There'll be no need."],["Victoria","Once the raid is successfully completed, regardless of whether Tiphys's book-thick preparation plan is completed or not, your council must pressure him to launch a full-scale attack."],["Victoria","Then, simply launch artillery strikes at the coordinates I've just outlined. We'll easily wipe out that mob..."],["Lukmund","What if you fail?"],["Victoria","Impossible."],["Lukmund","...Understood."],["","Lukmund nods thoughtfully, then extends his hand to Victoria."],["Lukmund","I may not be able to provide the Antibody squad you want... but I will introduce you to two other associates. If the operation is within Sankara, they should be able to offer more effective assistance."],["Victoria","Is that what you mean...? But unfortunately, my troops never accept traitors or captives."],["Lukmund","No, quite the opposite. Sometimes, the \"traitors\" are the most loyal to their homeland."],["Victoria","...Hmph."],["","After a moment of hesitation, Victoria still takes his hand."],["","If the locals' prediction is correct, then cooperating with Lukmund is my only option."],["","And she has a feeling... This man may be one of her kind."],["","Thinking about it now, if there is no real choice to begin with, then perhaps refusing to choose at all is the more reasonable decision."],["","She understands herself well. For someone like her, the last thing she needs is someone of the same kind."],["","The only thing she needs is someone to use."],["Victoria","...What's the situation?"],["Special Ops Deputy Captain","Still unable to contact Aiden and Vera. Almost at the same time, their whereabouts were discovered by Vesper."],["Victoria","At our current pace, it's only a matter of time before we're caught up."],["","With the more detailed map and enemy formation provided by Vera, the squad led by Victoria is able to choose a more secure route."],["","However, to avoid some patrol units, the squad cannot constantly maintain full speed and is now making a brief stop in the desert."],["Victoria","There are less than fifteen minutes left to the target location, and a more risky path must be taken."],["Special Ops Deputy Captain","Captain, a Vesper is approaching from five o'clock... We've been exposed."],["Arthur","Unknown forces ahead... No, DLAF ahead! Stop immediately, not another step!"],["Victoria","Just a squad of this size, is it? ...Everyone, prepare for battle."],["Victoria","We need to annihilate this squad within six minutes and then quickly break into the enemy command center."],["Victoria","We'll reclaim the DL's victory here and now."]],"468265301":[["","There's an overwhelming disparity in strength."],["","Forget the estimated six minutes... In just five minutes, the special forces crush Arthur's troops. Even with the prior impact of the battle with Aiden's forces, there remains an insurmountable gap between the two sides."],["","It's not just because of the PAMS System—this unit, selected and commanded by Victoria, possesses strength comparable to elite local forces. It's an impeccable weapon."],["","In the face of this enemy, Arthur recalls the times Cassha guided her in battle and command. Whenever she made a mistake, Cassha would only smile and give her gentle reminders..."],["","But in real combat, the price they paid was the death of their comrades."],["Victoria","Are you the one responsible for commanding this team?"],["Arthur","*huff, huff*"],["","Under Arthur's command, the remaining team members desperately maneuver their damaged STs, forming a defensive perimeter to block Victoria."],["","A wise choice... were it not foolish in the face of such power."],["Victoria","How pathetic... Get lost. Your claims, your rebellion—it's all futile."],["Arthur","That's something the Dawnstar League doesn't have the right to lecture us about!"],["Victoria","Don't compare me to the island's defense forces. From an outside perspective, all of this is just an opportunity."],["Arthur","You're from outside the island...?"],["","Before Arthur can cry out, Victoria's gun pierces through the cockpits of two more STs, further weakening this final stand..."],["Victoria","Even if you can awaken the so-called fighting spirit of the Milkhamans, what does it matter?"],["Victoria","Are you trying to recreate that initial struggle? Sacrificing yourself for that kind of future, then leaving the mess to the next generation?"],["Arthur","No, we will leave them the right to choose for themselves..."],["Victoria","Haha... What I want to tell you is, if we were to do it all over again, it wouldn't be like the last half-hearted war."],["Victoria","This time, there will be no concessions, no compromises, no ambiguity, no middle ground... This time, neither side has any so-called hope."],["Victoria","Only a true, comprehensive victory that completely crushes the other side can bring everything to rest."],["Victoria","Are you suggesting that the Milkhamans could be the ultimate victors?"],["Arthur","Hmm..."],["","Outside the island... Once she glimpses even a fragment of this immense power, the emotion she had long kept buried—fear—begins to creep back into Arthur's thoughts."],["","Because she knows the island so well, the more time she spends in its struggles, the more at home she feels—and that familiarity lets her confront each new challenge without fear."],["","Before the final battle arrives, as long as everyone is prepared and makes a concerted effort, death will not come knocking—or so she believes."],["","But now the concept of \"outside the island\" has emerged... like a shadow lurking beneath the sea suddenly leaping out of the water, effortlessly swallowing bait the size of Milkhama in a single gulp."],["","The challenges of narrowly escaping death time and again are nothing compared to a war of that scale."],["","Death doesn't come to them; it stands at the finish line, quietly waiting for them to cross over..."],["Victoria","Still unwilling to give up? Of course, you cowards would rather embrace death than face the destruction bearing down on you... the destruction you have created with your own hands."],["Arthur","I..."],["","Bang!!!"],["","Before Arthur can respond, Victoria has already fired."],["","Arthur tightly closes her eyes, but soon she realizes that the sound of breathing and the drumming of her heartbeat still echo in her ears."],["","She finds that she can still open her eyes. She is alive."],["Vesper Soldier","Captain... We have no regrets..."],["","A faint voice pulls her out of the confusion—and it isn't coming from the comms."],["","Through the gaping hole in the cockpit of the ST standing in her way, beneath the warped tangle of armor and cables, she sees a half-ruined body giving her a final farewell."],["","However, there is no expression of pain or fear on his face. Instead, he wears the calmness before battle, a calmness that seems almost out of place."],["","Death is not such an unbearable fact."],["Victoria","That guy..."],["Arthur","No... that's not it... How could I have forgotten...?"],["Arthur","The final victory... it doesn't matter even if we can't reach it..."],["Arthur","This was never what we were fighting for."],["","As her trembling hands gradually steady, Arthur takes a deep breath and tightly grips the control stick."],["","She raises her head, staring through the cockpit's broken hole, directly at Victoria's gun barrel, directly at her own future... Death."],["Arthur","It's not about resisting \"for\" something—the very act of resistance itself already has meaning."],["Arthur","We have always believed this."],["","She almost says it with a smile."],["Victoria","..."],["Victoria","Oh, really? Then just die."],["","Bang!!!"],["","This time, Arthur doesn't close her eyes. She stares death in the face and doesn't miss the moment that familiar figure arrives."],["Cassha","Sorry I'm late."],["","Accompanied by the sound of airborne troops whistling by, a familiar ST positions itself in front of her. In the surrounding dunes, one ST after another appears, gradually encircling Victoria's squad."],["Arthur","Cassha! Did you receive the alert?"],["Cassha","That's right, but I've also encountered quite a bit of trouble. Although compared to this..."],["Refugee A","Did I... Did I see that right? The DLAF really made it into Sankara!"],["Refugee B","No way... Could it be just like Aiden said, that Vesper is really helping us hold back the DLAF...?"],["","It is then that Arthur notices that among them are not only Vesper's STs but also quite a few from Sankara."],["Arthur","These locals are..."],["Cassha","It seems we've been misunderstood by Sankara in more than one area. After clearing up the misunderstanding, I brought them to here to help."],["Cassha","Without any declarations or regulations being issued, such DL infiltration operations won't receive any support..."],["Victoria","Damn, even these refugees are showing up?"],["","Victoria had long since prepared herself to fight to the very end. But among all the enemies she had envisioned, the forces of Sankara had never been one of them."],["","The moment these refugees are harmed in full view, the DL forfeits its strategic initiative in all subsequent stages of the war."],["Special Ops Deputy Captain","Captain, based on the current situation..."],["Victoria","...We have no choice but to retreat."],["Victoria","Will we have to leave this to Tiphys and his crew...? Tch, what a pain."],["","Half a day later, in a DL conference room..."],["Ma'at","Your Excellency, the Victoria squad has been defeated and is currently under investigation by Defense Force Headquarters."],["Ma'at","However, she has not disclosed any information related to you. As previously stated, she insists that this was the result of her own unilateral actions."],["Lukmund","Hmm... It really didn't work, hmm...?"],["Ma'at","...May I ask, did you foresee her failure in advance?"],["Lukmund","And you? Ma'at, what do you think of Victoria and her team?"],["Ma'at","She's strong... Although the probability wasn't high, she had the element of surprise."],["Lukmund","That's right, in a sense, her judgment was accurate... This kind of surprise attack was, in fact, the greatest effort the DL could muster."],["Lukmund","Plus, with the two I left in Sankara beforehand... Considering this, her success rate should be close to sixty percent, correct?"],["Ma'at","But you don't seem surprised at all by her failure."],["Lukmund","After all, if someone this reckless were to succeed so easily, then people like us... I'm afraid we wouldn't even qualify to sit at the table."],["Ma'at","If Victoria had succeeded, the Vesper defense line would have collapsed even before Tiphys launched a full-scale attack, making the struggle for the \"Legacy\" even more difficult... So, is this all part of your plan?"],["Lukmund","No, I just wanted to test if the others who are eagerly anticipating the war would just sit idly by... It seems they do have some tricks up their sleeves."],["Lukmund","However, Victoria's failure was not completely fruitless. At least it allowed us to understand the main angles of the internal situation of Sankara, which will facilitate your future actions..."],["","As he speaks, Lukmund rises from his seat and walks over to a nearby bookshelf. From a recessed slot hidden between the shelves, he retrieves a small locator receiver and hands it to Ma'at."],["Ma'at","This is..."],["Lukmund","This is my last card left in Sankara."],["Lukmund","Soon, everyone will be in their rightful place, and it will be my time to officially step onto the stage..."],["","In a facility hidden from all signal detection, a meeting is about to take place..."],["Skysweep","So... when's this so-called partner of ours finally gonna show up?"],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge... has been waiting for a long time..."],["Skysweep","You don't need to wait here with me, do you? We've got an actual intelligent conversation coming up here. A pyromaniac like you can just go back to base and pass the time playing with matches."],["Mirestomp","If only I could have fired a few more shots back then... I really want to face off against Cassha again..."],["Roarlash","Mirestomp, you didn't have permission to fire even then. You overstepped."],["Mirestomp","What do you even know? If we didn't strike first against her, there's no way we would've walked away in one piece."],["Roarlash","I was providing you with sniper support the entire time..."],["","Another typical argument among the Thunderbolt Squad. They can argue like this all day without repeating themselves, but for the upcoming meeting, a mediator has to step in and say a few words."],["Grimbite","Alright, everyone quiet down, he's here."],["","In fact, even without Grimbite stepping in, everyone had already noticed the approaching footsteps and stopped their bickering in unison."],["","The cheerful atmosphere dissipates, and a heavy silence envelops the space."],["","As the shadow gradually appears under the light, everyone's fingers rest on their triggers."],["Grimbite","As you requested, we ensured the survival of Vesper during the DL's full-scale attack. Now you must fulfill your promise."],["Yevgeny","Of course."],["","A briefcase made of pure black metal is placed on the table. Adorned with intricate Ovettian characters and numerous symbols representing danger, it warns all who approach."],["Grimbite","!!"],["Grimbite","How could it be... such a thing actually exists...?"],["Yevgeny","You, reshaped by the Nova-Frame, know all too well what this means."],["Grimbite","..."],["Grimbite","Hahaha..."],["Grimbite","Hahaha... and just as I was starting to get bored with the world. Seems I've got something worth looking forward to now, huh?!"],["","Grimbite pushes the briefcase in front of Goman. It is enough to confirm that what the other party described in the past truly exists."],["Grimbite","As expected, it was right to roll the dice..."],["Yevgeny","...Dice?"],["Grimbite","Nothing... You, Ovettian—I'm looking forward to working with you..."],["Grimbite","Let's start with the war, right?"],["Grimbite","Yes. For an opening act, that will suffice..."],["","Vesper Base"],["Arthur","..."],["Cassha","What's wrong? Something on your mind?"],["","After a brief respite, the entire base is once again plunged into intense preparations—the triumph from the last battle is short-lived."],["","But how could Arthur forget... That final farewell still echoes in her ears."],["","It is Cassha's voice that finally pulls her out of her daze."],["Arthur","No... it's nothing..."],["Cassha","You've been trying to tighten that screw for almost ten minutes. Do you need me to help you?"],["","The friendly jibe allows Arthur to relax a little."],["Arthur","...Cassha, they say it's always darkest before the dawn. Is that really true?"],["Cassha","Darkest before dawn, huh... Well... it's certainly encouraging. During the war, the Milkhamans reassured each other in the same way."],["Arthur","So now it's..."],["Cassha","Not yet, no."],["","Cassha flatly bursts Arthur's bubble, seemingly denying Vesper's achievements so far."],["","Yet still, she denies it directly."],["Cassha","If we were to use time as a metaphor... it's more like dusk before a long night."],["Cassha","The success we've achieved today might be the most brilliant accomplishment for years, or even decades to come..."],["Arthur","...Just as I feared."],["Cassha","Heh, isn't it obvious?"],["Arthur","How should I put it... Suddenly, it feels cruel..."],["Cassha","Indeed... but in my eyes, here and now, you all carry more courage and conviction than the Milkhamans ever did during the war."],["Cassha","Moving toward the light is something anyone can do... No, it's something everyone must do, as avoiding the darkness is instinctive."],["Cassha","And at this moment, Vesper is about to step out into the long night, into the darkness that never seems to end..."],["","Cassha crouches down, gently grasping Arthur's shoulders, calming the slightly trembling yet unwavering soul."],["Cassha","But don't worry, this courage to move forward—it's proof that you will make it through."],["Cassha","I promise you."],["","Arthur takes a deep breath, and any lingering doubts dissipate with Cassha's encouragement."],["","Yes, the night is long, and everything is just beginning."],["","But so what?"],["","They are ready."]]};
